<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nōmĭnālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		nomen, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a name, nominal</i>
			(ante- and postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gentilitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 8, § 4</span></i>
			 Müll.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nōmĭnālĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>the day on which a child received its name, the name-day</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Idol.
			16</span></i>.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nōmĭnālĭter</span></b> , <i>by name, expressly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annuere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 80</span></i>
			.</div>
